From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Incognito Lock

Build on Chromium's incognito lock (fingerprint, face or PIN to get
back to incognito tabs after leaving the app):

- It is on by default (it only works on devices with a screen lock;
  it can still be turned off in Settings > Privacy).
- "When to lock Incognito tabs" in the same settings: as soon as the
  user leaves CromIKO (the default), or 1, 5 or 15 minutes after. While
  the lock is on, changing it needs the screen lock, like turning the
  lock off. Tabs that were locked before the user left stay locked.
- "Lock Incognito tabs" in the app menu of incognito tabs and of the
  incognito tab switcher locks them right away.
- The lock screen shows the CromIKO mascot with a lock and "Your
  Incognito tabs are locked" instead of the incognito icon.
- Incognito tabs are hidden in the recent apps screen. Chromium already
  does this unless screenshots in incognito are allowed (the
  incognito-screenshot flag); with the lock on, CromIKO now hides them
  there even then (Android 13 and newer).

